    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5276": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - MC Family Medicine",
      "description": "Assistant Professor | LSUHSC Shreveport Tuesday, October 13, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Assistant Professor Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department MC Family Medicine Position Type Faculty Location Shreveport Description We are about creating exceptional experiences for both our patients and our employees. Partnering with the LSU School of Medicine, our goal is to provide high-quality patient care within a setting that advances medical science through research and educates the next generation of leaders in healthcare. We are committed to providing opportunities for our staff that develop and grow careers in a compassionate, team-oriented environment focused on patients first. At Ochsner LSU Health System of North Louisiana, whether you work with patients every day or support those who do, you are making a difference and that matters. Come make a difference at Ochsner LSU Health System of North Louisiana and discover your future today! LSU Health Sciences Center- Shreveport seeks applicants for an Assistant Professor position in the Department of Family Medicine. Opportunities exist at the Academic Medical Center as well as Community Clinics. Faculty members take an active role in teaching family medicine residents while maintaining a thriving clinical practice. Qualifications Applicant must meet the following: Must be board certified/board eligible in Family Medicine Eligible for active Louisiana Medical Licensure Preferred Qualifications N/A Additional Position Information PSN/PER Number: 28223/24-03-0259 Salary Range: Salary commensurate with experience and training Primary Location: Shreveport, LA About the School The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about 