    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5374": {
      "title": "Instructor/Assistant Professor - Clinical - MC Medicine Pediatrics",
      "description": "Instructor/Assistant Professor - Clinical | LSUHSC Shreveport Tuesday, October 13, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Instructor/Assistant Professor - Clinical Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department MC Medicine Pediatrics Position Type Faculty Location Shreveport Description Seeking an enthusiastic, successful, faculty member at the rank of Assistant Professor or Associate Professor (non-tenure, clinical track) for a clinical faculty position at LSU Health Shreveport. The selected candidate will participate in teaching medical students and residents in a clinical setting as well as in the private clinical setting. Qualifications The applicant must meet the following: Must be eligible for Louisiana medical licensure Must be board-certified or board-eligible with the American Board of Internal Medicine and American Board of Pediatrics Additional Position Information PSN/PER Number: PSN 54609/PER 24-07-0929 Salary Range: Commensurate with qualifications and experience. Primary Location: Shreveport, LA About the School The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about these benefits. Salary is commensurate with experience and training Generous Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Accidental Death & Dismemberment Insurance Flexible Spending Account Optional Retirement Plans LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Applicant Instructions To Apply : Locate and click on the A