    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5456": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor – Pediatric Gastroenterology - MC Pediatrics",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor – Pediatric Gastroenterology | LSUHSC Shreveport Tuesday, October 13, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Assistant/Associate Professor – Pediatric Gastroenterology Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department MC Pediatrics Position Type Faculty Location Shreveport Description The Department of Pediatrics at Louisiana State University Health Sciences Center (LSUHSC) in Shreveport is seeking a full-time BC/BE Pediatric Gastroenterologist. Primary responsibilities include a Pediatric Gastroenterology with patient care, resident and medical student education. Protected time is available to pursue clinical and/or laboratory research interests. Academic rank and salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Ochsner LSU Health St. Mary is the only major academic medical center in the area and receives patients from a catchment area with a radius of approximately 75-100 miles, which includes a population of approximately 1½ million people. The Pediatric Department is a large academic multispecialty department with active clinical and basic research programs. Shreveport is an attractive, comfortable, small southern city with excellent schools, good restaurants, and multicultural opportunities. It is an excellent place to raise children. Qualifications The applicant must meet the following: Must be eligible for LA Medical license Board Certified or Board Eligible in Pediatric Gastroenterology Additional Position Information PSN/PER Number: PSN 54483/PER 24-09-1281 Salary Range: Competitive and commensurate with experience Primary Location: Shreveport, LA About the School The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about these benefits. Salary is commensurate with experience and training Generous Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Accidental Death & Dismemberment Insurance Flexible Spending Account Optional Retirement Plans Applicant Instructions Locate and click on the Apply Online button located at the bottom of the screen, enter your contact information, and upload your resume/CV. If you need assistance applying electronically, please telephone 318-675-5589. If you are contacted for an interview, please let us know at that time if you will need special accommodations. Apply Online LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. LSU Health Shreveport has a goal of having at least 7% of our workers as people with disabilities. © 2026 LSUHSC Yes No"
    },
    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5468": {
      "title": "Instructor or Assistant Professor for Speech Language Pathology - MC Otolaryngology",
      "description": "Instructor or Assistant Professor for Speech Language Pathology | LSUHSC Shreveport Tuesday, October 13, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Instructor or Assistant Professor for Speech Language Pathology Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department MC Otolaryngology Position Type Faculty Location Shreveport Description The LSU Shreveport Department of Otolaryngology is seeking a Speech-Language Pathologist with advanced skill set and expertise working with the head and neck cancer population. The candidate must specialize in the diagnostics and management of swallowing, jaw opening, lymphatics, and speech in head and neck cancer patients undergoing surgery and/or radiation treatment. A medical speech-language pathologist (SLP) provides services for the prevention, identification, diagnosis, consultation, education, and rehabilitation of patients with acquired communication and swallowing disorders.  The SLP works closely with the patient, family, and other members of a physician-led team in providing individualized treatment. The candidate must have full competency with the swallowing diagnostics: videofluroscopic swallowing studies (MBS ImP, DIGEST) and fiberoptic endoscopic swallowing studies. The candidate must be comfortable working with multidisciplinary cancer team and holding weekly collaborations with our laryngologist and Head and Neck surgeons. Qualifications The applicant must meet the following: Master's degree in speech-language pathology Current Louisiana licensure as a Speech Language Pathologist Preferred Qualifications Advanced skill set and expertise working with the head and neck cancer population. The candidate must specialize in the diagnostics and management of swallowing, jaw opening, lymphatics, and speech in head and neck cancer patients undergoing surgery and/or radiation treatment. The ideal candidate would also have experience with laryngeal speech and pulmonary rehabilitation in the total laryngectomy population. Ideally, the candidate is familiar with clinical care pathways in head and neck cancer and holds certification/training with the following interventions: McNeill Dysphagia Therapy program, Pharyngocise, manual lymphatic drainage, and manual therapy/myofascial release. Certification of Clinical Competence in Speech-Language Pathology from the American Speech Language Hearing Association or academic equivalent with clinical fellowship year pending completion. Skilled in rigid and flexible video strobolaryngoscopy. Experience evaluating and treating adults with voice and voice related disorders Allied Health Staff in the Division of Speech Pathology are encouraged to achieve Board Certification by the Academy of Neurologic Communication Disorders and Sciences (BC-ANCDS) and/or awarded Board Certified Specialist in Swallowing and Swallowing Disorders by the American Board of Swallowing and Swallowing Disorders (BCS-S). Additional Position Information PSN/PER Number: PSN 58754/PER 24-10-1324 Salary Range: $90,000 - $94,000 Primary Location: Shreveport, LA (On-site position) About the School The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about these benefits. Salary is commensurate with experience and training Generous Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Accidental Death & Dismemberment Insurance Flexible Spending Account Optional Retirement Plans Applicant Instructions Locate and click on the Apply Online button located at the bottom of the screen, enter your contact information, and upload your resume/CV. If you need assistance applying electronically, please telephone 318-675-5589. If you are contacted for an interview, please let us know at that time if you will need special accommodations. Apply Online LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. LSU Health Shreveport has a goal of having at least 7% of our workers as people with disabilities. © 2026 LSUHSC Yes No"
    },
    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5469": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor - MC Otolaryngology",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor | LSUHSC Shreveport Tuesday, October 13, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Assistant/Associate Professor Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department MC Otolaryngology Position Type Faculty Location Shreveport Description LSU Health Shreveport is seeking a dynamic and highly motivated academic Otolaryngologist specializing in Head and Neck Surgery to join our growing team. The successful candidate will have the opportunity to shape and develop their academic career in a vibrant and collaborative academic health science center. This position is available at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor, depending on the qualifications and experience of the candidate. The Department of Otolaryngology at LSU Health Shreveport boasts a robust residency program and a Head and Neck Fellowship, providing a rich academic environment for both clinical practice and educational leadership. Clinical duties will include, but not be limited to, providing inpatient and outpatient clinical services to and developing a robust practice in Otolaryngology and Head and Neck Surgery covering call in rotation with fellow faculty members. Your work locations will include Ochsner LSU Health System of North Louisiana in Shreveport, Bossier City and Monroe as well as any other locations that the department covers. You must maintain your ability to perform clinical duties at Ochsner LSU Health System. Loss of privileges to practice at OLHS shall constitute cause and may result in termination of employment. You will be expected to fulfill your teaching/educational obligations throughout your employment at LSUHSC-Shreveport. Your responsibilities will include the responsibility as co-director of the Head and Neck Surgery Fellowship Program including teaching fellows, residents, and students. Expected to engage in scholarly activity including publications, have an active interest in research, and assist and engage fellows, residents and students with research projects. Qualifications The applicant must meet the following: MD or DO degree from an accredited medical school. Board certified/eligible in Otolaryngology – Head and Neck Surgery. Fellowship training in head and neck oncologic surgery. Eligibility for medical licensure in the state of Louisiana. Additional Position Information PSN/PER Number: PSN 27383/PER 24-10-1373 Salary Range: Competitive and commensurate with experience Primary Location: Shreveport, LA (On-site position) About the School The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about these benefits. Salary is commensurate with experience and training Generous Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Accidental Death & Dismemberment Insurance Flexible Spending Account Optional Retirement Plans Applicant Instructions Locate and click on the Apply Online button located at the bottom of the screen, enter your contact information, and upload your resume/CV. If you need assistance applying electronically, please telephone 318-675-5589. If you are contacted for an interview, please let us know at that time if you will need special accommodations. Apply Online LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. LSU Health Shreveport has a goal of having at least 7% of our workers as people with disabilities. © 2026 LSUHSC Yes No"
    },
    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5483": {
      "title": "Instructor/Assistant Professor Clinical - MC Medicine Endocrinology",
      "description": "Instructor/Assistant Professor Clinical | LSUHSC Shreveport Tuesday, October 13, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Instructor/Assistant Professor Clinical Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department MC Medicine Endocrinology Position Type Faculty Location Shreveport Description We are seeking a full-time physician at the Instructor or Assistant Professor level with an interest in adult Endocrinology to join a busy collegial academic practice serving north, central, and western Louisiana, as well as adjacent areas of Arkansas and Texas.  The practice sees patients with common and rare endocrine conditions and is supported by strong departments of Medical and Surgical Oncology, ENT-Head and Neck Surgery, Neurosurgery, Neuro-ophthalmology, Interventional and Diagnostic Radiology, and more. Applicants would be expected to participate in all faculty activities, including medical student, house staff and fellowship teaching responsibilities; patient care in outpatient clinics; in-patient consultations to hospital services including surgical services, ob-gyn, labor and delivery, and psychiatry; clinical or lab research; and community service. Qualifications The applicant must meet the following minimal standards: MD or equivalent terminal degree Qualify for a Louisiana medical license. BE/BC in Endocrinology, Diabetes and Metabolism. Preferred Qualifications Preferred qualifications include interest and experience in evidence-based practice, patient-centered care, and comfort with a wide range of patient backgrounds and medical sophistication. Additional Position Information PSN/PER Number: PSN 54081/PER 24-10-1313 Salary Range: Competitive and commensurate with experience Primary Location: Shreveport, LA (on-site position) About the School The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about these benefits. Salary is commensurate with experience and training Generous Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Accidental Death & Dismemberment Insurance Flexible Spending Account Optional Retirement Plans Applicant Instructions Locate and click on the Apply Online button located at the bottom of the screen, enter your contact information, and upload your resume/CV. If you need assistance applying electronically, please telephone 318-675-5589. If you are contacted for an interview, please let us know at that time if you will need special accommodations. Apply Online LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. LSU Health Shreveport has a goal of having at least 7% of our workers as people with disabilities. © 2026 LSUHSC Yes No"
    },
    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5484": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor Clinical - MC Urology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor Clinical | LSUHSC Shreveport Tuesday, October 13, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Assistant Professor Clinical Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department MC Urology Position Type Faculty Location Shreveport Description Primary responsibilities include patient care, resident education, and medical student education.  Clinical duties and responsibilities rotate among our tertiary Ochsner LSU Health Shreveport Academic Medical Center and two affiliated teaching institutions. Several da Vinci surgical systems (including a dual-console unit) are available for patient care and resident training. The successful applicant will join several full-time faculty members in a fully accredited Urology Residency Training Program. Academic rank and salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Ochsner LSU Health Shreveport, in conjunction with Ochsner LSU Health St. Mary, is the only major academic medical center in the area and receives patients from a catchment area with a radius of approximately 75-100 miles which includes a population of approximately 1½ million people. Shreveport is an attractive, comfortable, small southern city with excellent schools, good restaurants, and multicultural opportunities. It is an excellent place to raise children. Qualifications The applicant must meet the following: Must be BC/BE in Urology Eligible for LA Medical license Additional Position Information PSN/PER Number: PSN 56640/PER 24-09-1276 Salary Range: Competitive and commensurate with experience Primary Location: Shreveport, LA (on-site position) About the School The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about these benefits. Salary is commensurate with experience and training Generous Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Accidental Death & Dismemberment Insurance Flexible Spending Account Optional Retirement Plans Applicant Instructions Locate and click on the Apply Online button located at the bottom of the screen, enter your contact information, and upload your resume/CV. If you need assistance applying electronically, please telephone 318-675-5589. If you are contacted for an interview, please let us know at that time if you will need special accommodations. Apply Online LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. LSU Health Shreveport has a goal of having at least 7% of our workers as people with disabilities. © 2026 LSUHSC Yes No"
    },
    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5485": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Cardiology - MC EA Conway",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Cardiology | LSUHSC Shreveport Tuesday, October 13, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Assistant Professor - Cardiology Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department MC EA Conway Position Type Faculty Location Shreveport Description Louisiana State University Health Sciences Center- Shreveport seek to recruit one General Cardiology faculty with an interest in teaching, clinical and translational research. Appointment would be at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor. Must be BC/BE and eligible for Louisiana state medical licensure. The Division pf Cardiology is part of the Center of Excellence for Cardiovascular Diseases and Sciences with opportunities for collaborative research involving basic science and clinical departments. Seed money is available to support research for candidates with demonstrated interest in basic or translational research. Qualifications The applicant must meet the following: Have an MD, MD/PhD, DO, or international equivalent terminal degree, Be eligible for medical licensure and clinical practice in the state of Louisiana, Have a proven record of administrative and academic leadership abilities, as well as a demonstrated commitment to education and mentoring, Be eligible for faculty appointment at LSUHSC-Shreveport as an Assistant/Associate Professor, per SOM standards. Preferred Qualifications A strong record of scholarly achievement and extramural funding Demonstrated leadership and accomplishments in complex organizational environments Excellent communication skills to interface with learners, faculty, healthcare teams, administrators, and community organizations. Additional Position Information PSN/PER Number: 58794/24-09-1207 Salary: Commensurate with Experience Primary Location: Monroe, LA About the School The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. O