    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5600": {
      "title": "Section Chief - Cardiology - MC Medicine Cardiology",
      "description": "Section Chief - Cardiology | LSUHSC Shreveport Tuesday, October 13, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Section Chief - Cardiology Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department MC Medicine Cardiology Position Type Faculty Location Shreveport Description The Department of Internal Medicine at Louisiana State University Health Sciences Center in Shreveport is seeking a full-time Chief of the Section of Cardiology. This position will serve a critical role in the education of medical and allied health students, interns and residents in the Department of Medicine, fellows in the Section of Cardiology, and the faculty in the Section of Cardiology. The incumbent will serve as leader of the group of Cardiologists, advising the Chairperson regarding the hiring of faculty and staff and all other matters related to this group of physicians and staff employed within this group. The Chief of the Section of Cardiology will serve a critical role in the care of patients with cardiac illnesses, oversee the care of patients on the Cardiology service and in the Coronary Care Unit, provide consultative care to other physicians in the University regarding patients with Cardiac illnesses and undertake procedures needed for the care of patients with cardiac illnesses. Duties will include, but will not be limited to the following: Promoting clinical production and creating opportunities in all department sections Leading by example in clinical excellence and clinical productivity Maintaining the clinical schedule and ensuring coverage for all clinical areas Review and submission of annual financial reports and budget requests Optimization of clinic operations via appropriate staffing, cooperation with APPs/scheduling/nurses/MAs/staff, and resource utilization in conjunction with leadership Developing and monitoring goals and business plans for all department sections Creation, implementation and review of appropriate quality metrics for faculty Assisting in the development of community outreach resources and programs Participation in leadership discussions regarding operations, clinical needs/barriers, services, etc. Lead and supervise regularly scheduled educational meetings Maintain office hour availability M-F outside of clinical responsibilities Qualifications Candidates must have the following qualifications to be considered: Have an M.D. Be eligible for medical licensure and clinical practice in the state of Louisiana Board-Certified in the field of Cardiology Provide evidence of experience in the field of Cardiology Show competency in the interpretation of EKGs, echocardiograms, stress tests, cardiac catheterization, and other relevant tests, as well as the management of patients with cardiac illnesses, both acute and chronic Excellent communication skills to interface with learners, faculty, healthcare teams, administrators, community organizations and donors Preferred Qualifications The preferred candidate will also have the following: Proven record of administrative and academic leadership Demonstrated experience and accomplishments in Interventional Cardiology Candidates must be clinically active, highly motivated and possess the leadership skills necessary to ensure a commitment of excellence in all areas of the program. Additional Position Information PSN/PER Number: PSN 00028386/706 Salary Range: Competitive and commensurate with experience Primary Location: Shreveport, LA (On-site position) About the School The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about these benefits. LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Salary is commensurate with experience and training Generous Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Accidental Death & Dismemberment Insurance Flexible Spending Account Optional Retirement Plans Applicant Instructions Locate and click on the Apply Online button located at the bottom of the screen, enter your contact information, and upload your resume/CV. If you need assistance applying electronically, please telephone 318-675-5589. If you are contacted for an interview, please let us know at that time if you will need special accommodations. Apply Online LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. LSU Health Shreveport has a goal of having at least 7% of our workers as people with disabilities. © 2026 LSUHSC Yes No"
    },
    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5615": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Clinical – Pulmonary/Critical Care - MC EA Conway",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Clinical – Pulmonary/Critical Care | LSUHSC Shreveport Tuesday, October 13, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Assistant Professor - Clinical – Pulmonary/Critical Care Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department MC EA Conway Position Type Faculty Location Monroe Description Duties will include providing/supervising Pulmonary/Critical Care services to patients with in-house call to be determined by the Department Chairman along with involvement in other outside institutional endeavors. Also included is teaching/educational obligations throughout your employment. Consideration will be extended to all candidates who meet the required qualifications. Special interest will be directed to candidates who meet or exceed the needs of the department. Qualifications The applicant must meet the following: MD and/or DO Board certified/eligible in Pulmonary/Critical Care Licensed or eligible for licensure in the State of Louisiana A distinguished record in Pulmonary/Critical Care services Outstanding commensurate clinical activities Candidates must have a firm commitment to the education of residents and medical students Additional Position Information PSN/PER Number: PER 854 Salary: Commensurate with Experience Primary Location: Monroe, LA (on-site position) About the School The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about these benefits. The salary is commensurate with experience and training. Generous Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Accidental Death & Dismemberment Insurance Flexible Spending Account Optional Retirement Plans LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Applicant Instructions Locate and click on the Apply Online button located at the bottom of the screen, enter your contact information, and upload your resume/CV. If you need assistance applying electronically, please telephone 318-675-5589. If you are contacted for an interview, please let us know at that time if you will need special accommodations. Apply Online LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. LSU Health Shreveport has a goal of having at least 7% of our workers as people with disabilities. © 2026 LSUHSC Yes No"
    },
    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5621": {
      "title": "Section Chief - Medicine - MC Medicine",
      "description": "Section Chief - Medicine | LSUHSC Shreveport Tuesday, October 13, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Section Chief - Medicine Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department MC Medicine Position Type Faculty Location Shreveport Description Seeking experienced and motivated leader for Hospital Medicine Section within the Department of Medicine at LSU Health Shreveport, an integrated teaching hospital and health system in partnership with Ochsner Health. Position would include clinical work as a hospitalist, publishing the schedule for faculty hospitalists, creating/tracking/incentivizing quality metrics for the hospital medicine program. Responsibilities would also involve teaching house staff and medical students, ensuring learner evaluation completion, annual performance evaluations on all hospitalists. The position would include membership on the Medical Executive Committee of the hospital and expect other committee membership and participation. Qualifications The applicant must meet the following: Board certification or eligibility in Internal Medicine or Hospital Medicine by ABIM. Academic experience preferred but not required. Five years experience as a hospitalist. Excellent skills with regard to clinical medicine, leadership, communication, teaching. Additional Position Information PSN/PER Number: PSN 59182/PER 847 Salary Range: Competitive and commensurate with experience Primary Location: Shreveport, LA (on-site position) About the School The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about these benefits. Salary is commensurate with experience and training Generous Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Accidental Death & Dismemberment Insurance Flexible Spending Account Optional Retirement Plans LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Applicant Instructions Locate and click on the Apply Online button located at the bottom of the screen, enter your contact information, and upload your resume/CV. If you need assistance applying electronically, please telephone 318-675-5589. If you are contacted for an interview, please let us know at that time if you will need special accommodations. Apply Online LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. LSU Health Shreveport has a goal of having at least 7% of our workers as people with disabilities. © 2026 LSUHSC Yes No"
    },
    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5656": {
      "title": "Instructor or Assistant Professor (2 Positions) - MB Cellular Biology & Anatomy",
      "description": "Instructor or Assistant Professor (2 Positions) | LSUHSC Shreveport Tuesday, October 13, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Instructor or Assistant Professor (2 Positions) Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department MB Cellular Biology & Anatomy Position Type Faculty Location Shreveport Description The Department of Cellular Biology and Anatomy at LSU Health Shreveport, School of Medicine, is seeking a dedicated and student-centered educator to join our faculty as a full-time Instructor or Assistant Professor of Anatomy (non-tenure track). This is a 12-month faculty appointment beginning January 2, 2026. The successful candidate will play an integral role in the delivery of anatomical sciences across multiple academic programs, including the MD curriculum, School of Health Professions and Sciences (Allied Health), and graduate-level health professions education . Areas of teaching responsibility will include gross anatomy, neuroanatomy, histology, and embryology , in both lecture and cadaver-based laboratory settings. Faculty rank and salary will be commensurate with the candidate’s experience and academic credentials, in accordance with LSU Health Shreveport and LSU Board of Supervisors policies. Key Responsibilities Deliver high-quality instruction in gross anatomy, neuroanatomy, histology, and embryology. Participate in curriculum planning, development, delivery, and assessment. Collaborate in interdisciplinary and team-based teaching initiatives. Contribute to scholarly activity in anatomical education or biomedical sciences. Provide student mentoring and academic support. Serve on departmental and institutional committees as assigned. Qualifications The applicant must meet one of the following: Instructor Level: Master’s degree in Anatomy, Biological Sciences, or a related discipline, with cadaveric instruction experience. Assistant Professor Level: Terminal degree (PhD, MD, DO, or equivalent) in Anatomy or a related biomedical field, with evidence of scholarly contributions or potential. Demonstrated excellence in teaching at the undergraduate, graduate, or professional level. Strong interpersonal and communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching in medical or health sciences curricula. Demonstrated expertise in Gross Anatomy with proficiency in at least one additional anatomical science discipline, or strong expertise in Neuroanatomy with proficiency in at least one additional discipline. Experience in cadaveric dissection and prosection-based instruction. Familiarity with digital and virtual anatomy education tools. Interest in educational innovation, curriculum integration, or assessment. Additional Position Information PSN/PER Number: PSN 59278 & 59279/PER 1437 Salary Range: Competitive and commensurate with experience Primary Location: Shreveport, LA (On-Site) About the School The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about these benefits. Salary is commensurate with experience and training Generous Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Accidental Death & Dismemberment Insurance Flexible Spending Account Optional Retirement Plans LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Applicant Instructions Locate and click on the Apply Online button located at the bottom of the screen, enter your contact information and the following four items listed below: Cover letter describing interest and qualifications Curriculum Vitae Statement of teaching philosophy Contact information for three professional references If you need assistance applying electronically, please telephone 318-675-5589. If you are contacted for an interview, please let us know at that time if you will need special accommodations. Apply Online LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. LSU Health Shreveport has a goal of having at least 7% of our workers as people with disabilities. © 2026 LSUHSC Yes No"
    },
    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5699": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor Clinical - Cognitive Neurologist - MC Neurology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor Clinical - Cognitive Neurologist | LSUHSC Shreveport Tuesday, October 13, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Assistant Professor Clinical - Cognitive Neurologist Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department MC Neurology Position Type Faculty Location Shreveport Description LSU Health in Shreveport, Louisiana seeks a Board-Certified/Board-Eligible (BC/BE) Cognitive Specialist to join our outstanding Academic Neurology department and dynamic team. Leadership opportunities available to qualified candidates. We invite applications for the following position: Position: Full-time Academic faculty Academic Rank: Determined based on level of experience and qualifications Description : Open to BC/BE Neurologists with a commitment to both patient care and academic growth. The successful candidate will be a dynamic Cognitive/Dementia Specialist. Leadership opportunities available depending on qualifications. Key Responsibilities: Delivering high-quality clinical care to patients with neurological conditions. Medical student and Neurology resident education, including supervision in clinics, grand rounds, and didactic conferences. Participation in departmental activities and contributing to the growth of the Dementia program. Mentoring and providing clinical expertise to faculty and residents. Large patient volume potential and leadership potential. Louisiana has the 5 th highest Alzheimer’s mortality rate in the US and North Louisiana has a particularly large burden of disease. Potential to be the expert in the field in this region. Resources & Facilities: Dedicated Infusion Center Multi-disciplinary Care Academic Medical department with the largest concentration of Subspecialty Neurologists in the Ark-La-Tex region. School of Medicine Faculty and collaborations with the Graduate School and Allied Health Compensation and Benefits: Competitive salary package, including a guaranteed base salary. Supplemental pay based on productivity and potential grant funding. Opportunities for academic and professional development. J-1 visa sponsorship is available. Qualifications The applicant must meet the following: BC/BE Neurologist Preferred Qualifications Cognitive/Dementia Specialist Additional Position Information PSN/PER Number: PSN 59346/PER 1362 Salary Range: Competitive and commensurate with experience Primary Location: Shreveport, LA (on-site position) About the School The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about these benefits. Salary is commensurate with experience and training Generous Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Accidental Death & Dismemberment Insurance Flexible Spending Account Optional Retirement Plans LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Applicant Instructions Letters of interest and CV should be directed to: Chen Lin, MD, MBA Professor and Chair, Department of Neurology LSU Health Sciences Center 1501 Kings Hwy., Shreveport, LA 71103 Email: chen.lin@lsuhs.edu Apply Online LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. LSU Health Shreveport has a goal of having at least 7% of our workers as people with disabilities. © 2026 LSUHSC Yes No"
    },
    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5700": {
      "title": "Neuromuscular Neurologist - Division Chief - MC Neurology",
      "description": "Neuromuscular Neurologist - Division Chief | LSUHSC Shreveport Tuesday, October 13, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Neuromuscular Neurologist - Division Chief Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department MC Neurology Position Type Faculty Location Shreveport Description LSU Health in Shreveport, Louisiana seeks a Board-Certified/Board-Eligible (BC/BE) Neuromuscular Specialist to join our outstanding Academic Neurology department and dynamic team. Leadership opportunities available to qualified candidates. We invite applications for the following position: Position: Full-time Academic faculty Academic Rank: Determined based on level of experience and qualifications Key Responsibilities: Delivering high-quality clinical care to patients with neurological conditions. Medical student and Neurology resident education, including supervision in clinics, grand rounds, and didactic conferences. Participation in departmental activities and contributing to the growth of the Neuromuscular program. Mentoring and providing clinical expertise to faculty and residents. Qualifications Open to BC/BE Neurologists with a commitment to both patient care and academic growth. The successful candidate will by a dynamic Neuromuscular Specialist. Leadership opportunities available depending on qualifications. Preferred Qualifications Resources & Facilities: Dedicated Infusion Center Multi-disciplinary Care Academic Medical department with the largest concentration of Subspecialty Neurologists in the Ark-La-Tex region. School of Medicine Faculty and collaborations with the Graduate School and Allied Health Additional Position Information Salary Range: About the School Ochsner LSU Health Shreveport, in conjunction with Ochsner LSU Health St. Mary, is the only major academic medical center in the area and receives patients from a catchment area with a radius of approximately 75-100 miles which includes a population of approximately 1½ million people. Shreveport is an attractive, comfortable, small southern city with excellent schools, good restaurants, and multicultural opportunities. It is an excellent place to raise children. LSU Health Shreveport is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about these benefits. Salary is commensurate with experience and training Competitive salary package, including a guaranteed base salary. Generous Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Accidental Death & Dismemberment Insurance Flexible Spending Account Optional Retirement Plans Supplemental pay based on productivity and potential grant funding. Opportunities for academic and professional development. J-1 visa sponsorship is available. Potential for startup package for qualified candidates Applicant Instructions To Apply : Locate and click on the Apply Online button located at the bottom of the screen, enter your contact information, and upload your resume/CV. If you need assistance applying electronically, please telephone 318-675-5589. After submitting your application, please complete the following: Please send curriculum vitae, a statement of current interests, CV and names of three references to: Chen Lin, MD, MBA Professor and Chair, Department of Neurology LSU Health Sciences Center 1501 Kings Hwy., Shreveport, LA 71103 Email: chen.lin@lsuhs.edu If you are contacted for an interview, please let us know at that time if you will need special accommodations. Apply Online LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. LSU Health Shreveport has a goal of having at least 7% of our workers as people with disabilities. © 2026 LSUHSC Yes No"
