    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5721": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Research - MB Pharmacology & Toxicology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Research | LSUHSC Shreveport Tuesday, October 13, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Assistant Professor - Research Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department MB Pharmacology & Toxicology Position Type Faculty Location Shreveport Description The Department of Pharmacology, Toxicology & Neuroscience at LSU Health Shreveport invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor Research. The Research Assistant Professor will be engaged in a multidisciplinary research program in behavioral pharmacology and neuropharmacology and human subjects research in collaboration with Dr. Kevin Murnane at the School of Medicine, Louisiana State University Health Sciences Center. The research involves preclinical and translational studies designed to develop and evaluate novel drug formulations, new drug therapies, and underlying disease mechanisms, focused on substance use disorders, but aligned with co-occurring sleep, mood, pain, and neurodegenerative disorders. The individual will oversee a research team conducting behavioral studies in laboratory rodents, including drug self-administration, pharmacokinetics, assays of sleep and sedation, and tests of anxiety and affective behavior. These preclinical investigations are integrated with ongoing and planned human clinical trials and brain imaging studies, including functional MRI (fMRI) and PET imaging, to validate mechanistic insights and therapeutic efficacy across species that are being conducted by additional staff, predoctoral fellows, and post-doctoral fellows in the laboratory. The ultimate goal is to establish translational continuity from bench to bedside, facilitating the progression of promising candidates into clinical testing. In addition to laboratory research, the Research Assistant Professor will play a leadership role in developing new applications for extramural funding, supporting the regulatory advancement of candidate therapies, and contributing to regulatory documentation for pre-IND and IND submissions. Experience in data analysis, grant and manuscript writing, project management, and meeting critical milestones under tight timelines is essential. The ideal candidate will have a strong background in neuroscience and pharmacology, with opportunities to expand their expertise. Dr. Murnane will serve as a close mentor and collaborator to support the career development of the Research Assistant Professor while ensuring effective management of the research program. The candidate must be capable of independent project leadership and will also contribute to the mentorship of graduate students and trainees engaged in the program. Regular attendance is required to perform the functions of this position.  The work hours are generally Monday through Friday from 8:00AM to 5:00PM. Qualifications A doctoral degree (Ph.D. and/or M.D.) in pharmacology, neuroscience, toxicology, or a related biomedical field from an accredited institution. A minimum of two years of professional postdoctoral experience, an outstanding publication record, and a clear research focus in the areas mentioned above. Additional Position Information PSN/PER Number: PSN 27816/PER 1515 Salary Range: $80,000 - $110,000 Primary Location: Shreveport, LA (on-site) About the School The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about these benefits. Salary is commensurate with experience and training Generous Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Accidental Death & Dismemberment Insurance Flexible Spending Account Optional Retirement Plans Applicant Instructions Locate and click on the Apply Online button located at the bottom of the screen, enter your contact information, and upload your resume/CV. If you need assistance applying electronically, please telephone 318-675-5589. If you are contacted for an interview, please let us know at that time if you will need special accommodations. Apply Online LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. LSU Health Shreveport has a goal of having at least 7% of our workers as people with disabilities. © 2026 LSUHSC Yes No"
    },
    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5725": {
      "title": "Associate Professor Clinical - Comprehensive Neurologist-Division Chief - MC Neurology",
      "description": "Associate Professor Clinical - Comprehensive Neurologist-Division Chief | LSUHSC Shreveport Tuesday, October 13, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Associate Professor Clinical - Comprehensive Neurologist-Division Chief Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department MC Neurology Position Type Faculty Location Shreveport Description LSU Health in Shreveport, Louisiana seeks a Board-Certified/Board-Eligible (BC/BE) Neurologist to join our outstanding Academic Neurology department and dynamic team. Leadership opportunities available to qualified candidates. We invite applications for the following position: Position: Full-time Academic faculty Academic Rank: Determined based on level of experience and qualifications Description : Open to BC/BE Neurologists with a commitment to both patient care and academic growth. The successful candidate will be a dynamic General Neurologist. Leadership opportunities available depending on qualifications. Key Responsibilities: Delivering high-quality clinical care to patients with neurological conditions. Medical student and Neurology resident education, including supervision in clinics, grand rounds, and didactic conferences. Participation in departmental activities and contributing to the growth of the Dementia program. Mentoring and providing clinical expertise to faculty and residents. Large patient volume potential and leadership potential. Resources & Facilities: Dedicated Infusion Center Multi-disciplinary Care Academic Medical department with the largest concentration of Subspecialty Neurologists in the Ark-La-Tex region. School of Medicine Faculty and collaborations with the Graduate School and Allied Health Compensation and Benefits: Competitive salary package, including a guaranteed base salary. Supplemental pay based on productivity and potential grant funding. Opportunities for academic and professional development. J-1 visa sponsorship is available. Qualifications The applicant must meet the following: BC/BE Neurologist Additional Position Information PSN/PER Number: PSN 59380/PER 1647 Salary Range: Competitive and commensurate with experience. Primary Location: Shreveport, LA (on-site position) About the School Ochsner LSU Health Shreveport, in conjunction with Ochsner LSU Health St. Mary, is the only major academic medical center in the area and receives patients from a catchment area with a radius of approximately 75-100 miles which includes a population of approximately 1½ million people. Shreveport is an attractive, comfortable, small southern city with excellent schools, good restaurants, and multicultural opportunities. It is an excellent place to raise children. The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about these benefits. Salary is commensurate with experience and training Generous Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Accidental Death & Dismemberment Insurance Flexible Spending Account Optional Retirement Plans LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Applicant Instructions Letters of interest and CV should be directed to: Chen Lin, MD, MBA Professor and Chair, Department of Neurology LSU Health Sciences Center 1501 Kings Hwy., Shreveport, LA 71103 Email: chen.lin@lsuhs.edu Apply Online LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. LSU Health Shreveport has a goal of having at least 7% of our workers as people with disabilities. © 2026 LSUHSC Yes No"
    },
    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5734": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Professor - Tenure Track - MB Cellular Biology & Anatomy",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate/Professor - Tenure Track | LSUHSC Shreveport Tuesday, October 13, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Assistant/Associate/Professor - Tenure Track Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department MB Cellular Biology & Anatomy Position Type Faculty Location Shreveport Description The Department of Cellular Biology and Anatomy at LSU Health Shreveport invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant Professor, Associate Professor or Professor level. We seek outstanding scientists to establish an innovative, extramurally funded research program that advances understanding of cardiac pathophysiology. PhD + relevant postdoc experience. Our Cardiac Biology Research Group has internationally recognized strengths in fibroblast biology and fibrosis, HFrEF modeling (MI, I/R, TAC), cardio-oncology, cardio-immunology, and hiPSC-derived disease modeling. All cardiac researchers are welcome to apply, but we are particularly interested in candidates who will complement and expand our expertise in: Cardiac electrophysiology and calcium handling Sarcomere biology and force generation HFpEF modeling Translational research bridging basic and clinical science Faculty will benefit from strong institutional support and integration with the Center for Cardiovascular Diseases and Sciences, WWW.LSU_Shreveport-CCDS, which offers exceptional opportunities for collaboration in vascular biology, including atherosclerosis, metabolic dysfunction-associated steatohepatitis, neurovascular injury/stroke, peripheral artery disease, and microvascular dysfunction. Responsibilities include: Leading an innovative and sustainable research program supported by NIH R01 or equivalent funding. NIH K99 awardees are welcome to apply. Publishing impactful findings in high-quality journals and presenting at national/international conferences Teaching and mentoring graduate students, postdoctoral fellows, medical students, and residents Contributing to departmental and institutional service and fostering a collaborative scientific environment Regular attendance is required to perform the functions of this position.  The work hours are generally Monday through Friday from 8:00AM to 5:00PM. Qualifications Applicant must have a PhD with relevant Postdoctoral experience and extramural NIH funding, preferably at the R01 level, but at a minimum as a K99/R00 award. Additional Position Information PSN/PER Number: PSN 59431/PER 1592 Salary Range: Salary is commensurate with experience and training. Primary Location: Shreveport, LA (on-site) About the School The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about these benefits. Salary is commensurate with experience and training Generous Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Accidental Death & Dismemberment Insurance Flexible Spending Account Optional Retirement Plans Applicant Instructions Locate and click on the Apply Online button located at the bottom of the screen, enter your contact information and submit: cover letter, curriculum vitae, statements of research and teaching interests and contact information for at least three references. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For further inquiry, please contact the Department head, Dr. Hind Lal (hind.lal@lsuhs.edu). If you need assistance applying electronically, please telephone 318-675-5589. Apply Online LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. LSU Health Shreveport has a goal of having at least 7% of our workers as people with disabilities. © 2026 LSUHSC Yes No"
    },
    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5774": {
      "title": "Physician – Rheumatologist – Full Time Academic - MC Medicine Rheumatology",
      "description": "Physician – Rheumatologist – Full Time Academic | LSUHSC Shreveport Tuesday, October 13, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Physician – Rheumatologist – Full Time Academic Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department MC Medicine Rheumatology Position Type Faculty Location Shreveport Description Ochsner LSU Health System and Louisiana State University Health Sciences Center- Shreveport seeks a Fellowship-trained Rheumatologist in the Division of Rheumatology.  Must be board certified/ board eligible in Rheumatology and be eligible for active Louisiana Medical Licensure. The incumbent will be expected to direct patient care, conduct substantial and meaningful research; teach residents and medical students; and perform public and University service. Excellent teaching is an essential criterion for appointment in this series. Priority will be given to candidates with a proven track record of academic productivity, as demonstrated through high-impact publications, thematic-based research, and/or grant funding. The successful candidate will be expected to deliver patient care in an academic setting, teach medical students, residents, and fellows, engage in an independent and extramurally funded clinical research program, and provide service to the University. Rank and salary will be commensurate with training, qualifications, and experience. Expertise in the following rheumatic diseases: Rheumatoid arthritis. Systemic lupus erythematosus. Spondyloarthropathies including ankylosing spondylitis, psoriatic arthritis, reactive arthritis and enteropathic arthritis. Inflammatory myositis. Systemic sclerosis. Gout and calcium pyrophosphate dihydrate deposition disease. Behcet’s disease. Systemic sarcoidosis. Rheumatic complications in transplant medicine. Qualifications Have an MD, MD/PhD, DO or international equivalent terminal degree. Be eligible for medical licensure and clinical practice in the state of Louisiana. Have a proven record of administrative and academic leadership abilities, as well as a demonstrated commitment to education and mentoring. Be eligible for faculty appointment at LSUHSC-Shreveport as an Associate Professor or above, per SOM standards. Preferred Qualifications A strong record of scholarly achievement and extramural funding. Excellent communication skills to interface with learners, faculty, healthcare teams, administrators, community organizations and donors. We are especially interested in qualified candidates who can contribute, through their research, teaching, and/or service, to the diversity and excellence of the academic community and will work toward building an equitable and diverse scholarly environment. Additional Position Information PSN/PER Number: PSN 28440/PER 1350 Salary Range: $90,000 - $110,000 Primary Location: Shreveport, LA (on-site) About the School The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about these benefits. Salary is commensurate with experience and training Generous Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Accidental Death & Dismemberment Insurance Flexible Spending Account Optional Retirement Plans Applicant Instructions Locate and click on the Apply Online button located at the bottom of the screen, enter your contact information, and upload your resume/CV. If you need assistance applying electronically, please telephone 318-675-5589. If you are contacted for an interview, please let us know at that time if you will need special accommodations. Apply Online LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. LSU Health Shreveport has a goal of having at least 7% of our workers as people with disabilities. © 2026 LSUHSC Yes No"
