    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5818": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - MB Physiology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor | LSUHSC Shreveport Tuesday, October 13, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Assistant Professor Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department MB Physiology Position Type Faculty Location Shreveport Description The Department of Molecular & Cellular Physiology invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the level of Assistant Professor. Successful applicants will be expected to develop an independent, nationally funded research program. Preference will be given to individuals with extramural funding (such as NIH K99/R00 or R01) in cancer research, but consideration also will be given to those funded in other areas complimentary to those of the department, including cardiovascular, neurovascular, or metabolic disease. Information about departmental research focus areas is available at www.lsuhs.edu/departments/school-of-graduate-studies/molecular-and-cellular-physiology . A generous startup package and appropriate space will be offered. Qualifications Applicant must meet the following: Doctoral degree in physiology or a related biomedical field from an accredited institution. Two (2) years of professional, postdoctoral experience. Additional Position Information PSN/PER Number : PSN 59658/PER 2794 Salary Range: Commensurate with experience Primary Location: Shreveport, LA (on-site) About the School The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about these benefits. Salary is commensurate with experience and training Generous Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Accidental Death & Dismemberment Insurance Flexible Spending Account Optional Retirement Plans Generous startup package Dedicated laboratory space and state-of-the-art core facilities Intramural funding opportunities LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Information about the Department is provided at: https://schoolofgradstudies.lsuhs.edu/academics/molecular-and-cellular-physiology Applicant Instructions Locate and click on the Apply Online button located at the bottom of the screen, enter your contact information, and upload your letter of interest, CV, future research plans, and contact information for three professional references. If you need assistance applying electronically, please telephone 318-675-5589. Questions regarding the Department can be addressed to: Norman R. Harris, PhD Email: norman.harris@lsuhs.edu Apply Online LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. LSU Health Shreveport has a goal of having at least 7% of our workers as people with disabilities. © 2026 LSUHSC Yes No"
