    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5838": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Clinical - MC Medicine Pediatrics",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Clinical | LSUHSC Shreveport Tuesday, October 13, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Assistant Professor - Clinical Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department MC Medicine Pediatrics Position Type Faculty Location Shreveport Description The Department of Internal Medicine at Louisiana State University Health Sciences Center in Shreveport is seeking a full-time Assistant Professor in the Section of Medicine-Pediatrics. This position will include outpatient clinic service and serving as consulting faculty on the clinical services staffed by the Department of Medicine, Section of Medicine-Pediatrics. The incumbent will have responsibilities for teaching and mentoring students, residents and fellows and may attend on the Medicine ward services as needed. Qualifications The applicant must meet the following: Have an M.D. Be eligible for medical licensure and clinical practice in the state of Louisiana Board-Certified/Board Eligible in Internal Medicine Provide evidence of experience in the field of Internal Medicine Additional Position Information PSN/PER Number: PSN 59742/PER 2770 Salary Range: $94,000-$125,000 Primary Location: Shreveport, LA (On-Site) About the School The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about these benefits. Salary is commensurate with experience and training Generous Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Accidental Death & Dismemberment Insurance Flexible Spending Account Optional Retirement Plans Applicant Instructions To Apply : Locate and click on the Apply Online button located at the bottom of the screen, enter your contact information, and upload your resume/CV. If you need assistance applying electronically, please telephone 318-675-5589. If you are contacted for an interview, please let us know at that time if you will need special accommodations. Apply Online LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. LSU Health Shreveport has a goal of having at least 7% of our workers as people with disabilities. © 2026 LSUHSC Yes No"
    },
    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5841": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor - Urologic Oncology - MC Urology",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor - Urologic Oncology | LSUHSC Shreveport Tuesday, October 13, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Assistant/Associate Professor - Urologic Oncology Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department MC Urology Position Type Faculty Location Shreveport Description The Department of Urology at Louisiana State University Health Sciences Center in Shreveport is seeking a full-time BC/BE Urologist, Fellowship trained Urologic Oncology to expand its full-time clinical faculty. Primary responsibilities include patient care, resident education, and medical student education.  Clinical duties and responsibilities rotate among our tertiary Ochsner LSU Health Shreveport Academic Medical Center and two affiliated teaching institutions. Several da Vinci surgical systems (including a dual-console unit) are available for patient care and resident training. The successful applicant will join several full-time faculty members in a fully accredited Urology Residency Training Program. Academic rank and salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Ochsner LSU Health Shreveport, in conjunction with Ochsner LSU Health St. Mary, is the only major academic medical center in the area and receives patients from a catchment area with a radius of approximately 75-100 miles which includes a population of approximately 1½ million people. Shreveport is an attractive, comfortable, small southern city with excellent schools, good restaurants, and multicultural opportunities. It is an excellent place to raise children. Qualifications The applicant must meet the following: BE/BC in Urology Eligible for LA Medical license Additional Position Information PSN/PER Number: PSN 33476/PER 1386 Salary Range: Commensurate with qualifications and experience. Primary Location: Shreveport, LA (On-Site) About the School The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about these benefits. Salary is commensurate with experience and training Generous Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Accidental Death & Dismemberment Insurance Flexible Spending Account Optional Retirement Plans Applicant Instructions To Apply : Locate and click on the Apply Online button located at the bottom of the screen, enter your contact information, and upload your resume/CV. If you need assistance applying electronically, please telephone 318-675-5589. If you are contacted for an interview, please let us know at that time if you will need special accommodations. Apply Online LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. LSU Health Shreveport has a goal of having at least 7% of our workers as people with disabilities. © 2026 LSUHSC Yes No"
