    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5845": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - AH Cardiopulmonary Science",
      "description": "Assistant Professor | LSUHSC Shreveport Tuesday, October 13, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Assistant Professor Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department AH Cardiopulmonary Science Position Type Faculty Location Shreveport Description This position will work in a classroom and/or clinical (bedside) teaching capacity with undergraduate cardiopulmonary science and cardiovascular technology students. This person is to function as a full-time faculty member in the Department of Cardiopulmonary Science as directed by the Department Chair and/or Program Director or his/her designee. The incumbent will contribute to the academic development of any and all students within the Dept. of Cardiopulmonary Science. Primary responsibilities include teaching didactic courses, student labs, and developing innovative lecture/lab material. This position also includes the guidance of CPS/CVT/RT program students, collaborating with clinical affiliates, participating in program accreditation, developing assessments, engaging in program/School recruitment activities, participating in faculty development and professional development, and engaging in scholarly activity. Regular attendance is required to perform the functions of this position. Qualifications Applicant must meet one of the following qualifications: Bachelor's degree from an accredited university in science, or a related healthcare field with at least five (5) years of professional post-graduate experience in a professional, clinical setting. Master’s degree preferred. Credentialed in cardiovascular care. Preferred Qualifications Experienced echocardiography professional with participation in invasive cardiovascular patient care. Experienced invasive cardiovascular care professional with participation in non-invasive cardiovascular patient care. Three (3) or more years of experience teaching in an accredited clinical program. Additional Position Information PSN/PER Number: PSN 59805/PER 3016 Salary Range: $60,000 - $70,000 Primary Location: Shreveport, LA (On-Site About the School The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about these benefits. Salary is commensurate with experience and training Generous Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Accidental Death & Dismemberment Insurance Flexible Spending Account Optional Retirement Plans Applicant Instructions To Apply : Locate and click on the Apply Online button located at the bottom of the screen, enter your contact information, and upload your resume/CV. If you need assistance applying electronically, please telephone 318-675-5589. If you are contacted for an interview, please let us know at that time if you will need special accommodations. Apply Online LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. LSU Health Shreveport has a goal of having at least 7% of our workers as people with disabilities. © 2026 LSUHSC Yes No"
