    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5847": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Clinical Pediatrics - MC EA Conway",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Clinical Pediatrics | LSUHSC Shreveport Tuesday, October 13, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Assistant Professor of Clinical Pediatrics Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department MC EA Conway Position Type Faculty Location Monroe Description Duties will include providing/supervising Pediatric services to outpatient and in-patient setting and assist with in-house call to be determined by the Department Chairman along with involvement in other outside institutional endeavors. Also included are teaching and educational obligations throughout your employment. Consideration will be extended to all candidates who meet the required qualifications. Special interest will be directed to candidates who meet or exceed the needs of the department. Qualifications The applicant must meet the following: MD and/or DO Board certified/eligible in Pediatrics Licensed or eligible for licensure in the State of Louisiana A distinguished record in Pediatrics Commensurate clinical activities Candidates must have a firm commitment to the education of residents and medical students Additional Position Information PSN/PER Number: PSN 27711/PER 2963 Salary: Commensurate with Experience Primary Location: Monroe, LA (On-Site) About the School The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about these benefits. The salary is commensurate with experience and training. Generous Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Accidental Death & Dismemberment Insurance Flexible Spending Account Optional Retirement Plans LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Applicant Instructions To Apply : Locate and click on the Apply Online button located at the bottom of the screen, enter your contact information, and upload your resume/CV. If you need assistance applying electronically, please telephone 318-675-5589. If you are contacted for an interview, please let us know at that time if you will need special accommodations. Apply Online LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. LSU Health Shreveport has a goal of having at least 7% of our workers as people with disabilities. © 2026 LSUHSC Yes No"
    },
    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5854": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor - Tenure Track (2 Positions) - MC Neurology",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor - Tenure Track (2 Positions) | LSUHSC Shreveport Tuesday, October 13, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Assistant/Associate/Full Professor - Tenure Track (2 Positions) Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department MC Neurology Position Type Faculty Location Shreveport Description The Institute for Cerebrovascular and Neuroregeneration Research (ICNR) in the Department of Neurology at LSU Health Shreveport invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. Under the leadership of the new Neurology Chair, Dr. Chen Lin, and Vice Chair of Research, Dr. Quanguang Zhang, the department is undergoing rapid growth. Our faculty are engaged in cutting-edge research spanning cerebrovascular and neuroregenerative diseases, Alzheimer’s disease and related dementias, neurological and psychiatric disorders, as well as pharmacological and non-invasive therapeutic approaches. These efforts aim to elucidate disease pathogenesis and guide the development of mechanistic studies and novel therapeutic strategies for brain injury and neurodegenerative diseases. Successful candidates will be expected to establish and sustain an independent, extramurally funded research program. Preference will be given to applicants with a strong record of scholarship and demonstrated expertise in cerebrovascular science, neurobiology, neuroscience, or neurodegenerative diseases. More information on the department’s research areas can be found here: LSUHS Neurology Research – ICNR: https://www.lsuhs.edu/departments/school-of-medicine/neurology/research/institute-for-cerebrovascular-and-neuroregeneration-research Qualifications The applicant must meet the following: A doctoral degree (Ph.D. and/or M.D.) in neuroscience or a related biomedical field from an accredited institution. A minimum of two years of postdoctoral experience. An outstanding record of publications and a clear research focus aligned with the areas listed above. An active NIH grant or equivalent national funding. Preferred Qualifications Expertise in molecular biology, genetics, or electrophysiology/EEG. Additional Position Information PSN/PER Number: PSN 59823, 59824/PER 3084 Salary Range: Competitive and commensurate with experience. Primary Location: Shreveport, LA (On-Site) About the School The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about these benefits. Salary is commensurate with experience and training Generous Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Accidental Death & Dismemberment Insurance Flexible Spending Account Optional Retirement Plans Applicant Instructions To Apply : Locate and click on the Apply Online button located at the bottom of the screen, enter your contact information, and upload your resume/CV. If you need assistance applying electronically, please telephone 318-675-5589. After submitting your application, please complete the following: Please send curriculum vitae, a statement of current interests, and names of three references to: Chen Lin, MD, MBA Professor and Chair, Department of Neurology LSU Health Sciences Center 1501 Kings Hwy., Shreveport, LA 71103 Email: chen.lin@lsuhs.edu If you are contacted for an interview, please let us know at that time if you will need special accommodations. Apply Online LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. LSU Health Shreveport has a goal of having at least 7% of our workers as people with disabilities. © 2026 LSUHSC Yes No"
    },
    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5856": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Professor - Tenure Track - MB Microbiology & Immunology",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate/Professor - Tenure Track | LSUHSC Shreveport Tuesday, October 13, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Assistant/Associate/Professor - Tenure Track Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department MB Microbiology & Immunology Position Type Faculty Location Shreveport Description The Department of Microbiology and Immunology at LSU Health Shreveport invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor level. While the search is open at all ranks, we are especially interested in recruiting an exceptional early-career investigator poised to build a sustained and nationally visible research program. Candidates whose work bridges virology, immunology, and cancer biology are particularly encouraged to apply, including those studying virus-driven malignancy, antiviral and antitumor immune responses, virus-host interactions in the tumor microenvironment, or therapeutic development involving oncolytic or cancer-relevant viruses. The successful candidate will be expected to develop and maintain a nationally competitive, extramurally funded research program, participate in graduate and medical education, and contribute to the mentoring of Ph.D. students and postdoctoral fellows. LSU Health Shreveport offers a highly collaborative environment for investigators working at the intersection of virology, immunology, and cancer biology. The Department of Microbiology and Immunology has a long and successful track record in tumor virology and virus-host interaction research and identifies molecular and tumor virology among its core research strengths. Departmental faculty maintain NIH-funded programs in viruses, bacteria, and the immune system, and the department continues to expand its research and training enterprise. Candidates will also benefit from the broader cancer research environment at LSU Health Shreveport, including the Feist-Weiller Cancer Center (FWCC), a Center of Excellence that integrates cancer research, clinical care, and medical education. FWCC-supported institutional resources provide additional intramural funding for advancing cancer-related research programs. Additional collaborative opportunities are available through the Center for Applied Immunology and Pathological Processes (CAIPP), an NIH-funded COBRE center at LSU Health Shreveport. CAIPP provides access to an Immunophenotyping Core and a Bioinformatics and Modeling Core, supporting advanced flow cytometry, immunologic phenotyping, cell analysis, and omics/data science workflows. LSU Health Shreveport investigators also have access to extensive institutional research infrastructure and core facilities, including campus research cores and specialized shared resources that support modern biomedical research. Qualifications The applicant must meet the following: Ph.D., M.D., or M.D./Ph.D. Postdoctoral research training. An active, independently funded research program at the R01 or K99/R00 level in oncogenic viruses, oncolytic viruses, tumor immunology, or infection-associated cancer biology, preferably with a focus relevant to cancer/tumor biology. Additional Position Information PSN/PER Number: PSN 27911/PER 3017 Salary Range: Competitive and commensurate with experience. Primary Location: Shreveport, LA (On-Site) About the School The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about these benefits. Salary is commensurate with experience and training Generous Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Accidental Death & Dismemberment Insurance Flexible Spending Account Optional Retirement Plans Applicant Instructions To Apply : Locate and click on the Apply Online button located at the bottom of the screen, enter your contact information, and upload your resume/CV. If you need assistance applying electronically, please telephone 318-675-5589. Applicants should also submit: A cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of current and future research interests, statement of current funding, statement of teaching and mentoring interests, and contact information for three references. Application materials should be sent by email to: Matthew D. Woolard, Ph.D. Professor and Chair Department of Microbiology and Immunology LSU Health Shreveport matthew.woolard@lsuhs.edu Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. If you are contacted for an interview, please let us know at that time if you will need special accommodations. Apply Online LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. LSU Health Shreveport has a goal of having at least 7% of our workers as people with disabilities. © 2026 LSUHSC Yes No"
    },
    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5870": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Clinical - OB/GYN - MC Obstetrics & Gynecology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Clinical - OB/GYN | LSUHSC Shreveport Tuesday, October 13, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Assistant Professor - Clinical - OB/GYN Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department MC Obstetrics & Gynecology Position Type Faculty Location Shreveport Description Clinical responsibilities and duties will, in general, include, but are not limited to: providing gynecological services to patients in the Ob/Gyn Clinics including Ob/Gyn Faculty Clinic, Specialist Clinic, ACC, Bossier clinic, Monroe Hospital, and both Labor and Delivery Units. The bulk of the 40-hour weekly minimum productivity will be spent in the care of patients at Ochsner LSU Health Shreveport at 1541 Kings Highway, Shreveport, Ochsner LSU Health – St. Mary Medical Center at 915 Margaret Place, Shreveport, 2120 Bert Kouns, Shreveport, 1560 Irving Place, Shreveport, 2120 Airline Drive, Bossier City, 4864 Jackson St., Monroe, LA and assist with covering affiliated/contracted clinics across the greater metropolitan area. Qualifications The applicant must meet the following: Must be eligible for Louisiana medical licensure. Must be board-certified or board-eligible with the American Board of Obstetrics and Gynecology. Additional Position Information PSN/PER Number: PSN 59920/PER 3077 Salary Range: Competitive and commensurate with experience. Primary Location: Shreveport, LA (On-Site) About the School The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about these benefits. Salary is commensurate with experience and training Generous Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Accidental Death & Dismemberment Insurance Flexible Spending Account Optional Retirement Plans Applicant Instructions To Apply : Locate and click on the Apply Online button located at the bottom of the screen, enter your contact information, and upload your resume/CV. If you are contacted for an interview, please let us know at that time if you will need special accommodations. Apply Online LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. LSU Health Shreveport has a goal of having at least 7% of our workers as people with disabilities. © 2026 LSUHSC Yes No"
