    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5871": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor – Interventional Radiology - MC Radiology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor – Interventional Radiology | LSUHSC Shreveport Tuesday, October 13, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Assistant Professor – Interventional Radiology Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department MC Radiology Position Type Faculty Location Shreveport Description The Department of Radiology at Louisiana State University Health Sciences Center in Shreveport is seeking a full-time BC/BE Interventional Radiologist. Primary responsibilities include patient care, resident education, and medical student education.   Protected time is available to pursue clinical and/or laboratory research interests. Academic rank and salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Through our partnership with Ochsner LSU Health Shreveport and Ochsner LSU Health St. Mary, we provide the only major academic medical center in the area and receive patients from a catchment area with a radius of approximately 75-100 miles which includes a population of approximately 1½ million people. The Radiology Department is a large academic multispecialty Department with active clinical and basic research programs. Shreveport is an attractive, comfortable, small southern city with excellent schools, good restaurants, and multicultural opportunities. It is an excellent place to raise children. Qualifications The applicant must meet the following: Board Certified/Board Eligible Interventional Radiologist Licensed/eligible for LA Medical license Additional Position Information PSN/PER Number: PSN 56385/PER 3198 Salary Range: Competitive and commensurate with experience Primary Location: Shreveport, LA (On-Site) About the School About the Department/School: The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about these benefits. Salary is commensurate with experience and training Generous Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Accidental Death & Dismemberment Insurance Flexible Spending Account Optional Retirement Plans Applicant Instructions To Apply : Locate and click on the Apply Online button located at the bottom of the screen, enter your contact information, and upload your resume/CV. If you are contacted for an interview, please let us know at that time if you will need special accommodations. Apply Online LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. LSU Health Shreveport has a goal of having at least 7% of our workers as people with disabilities. © 2026 LSUHSC Yes No"
    },
    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5874": {
      "title": "Assistant Dean for Faculty Development - DA Student Aff-Medical",
      "description": "Assistant Dean for Faculty Development | LSUHSC Shreveport Tuesday, October 13, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Assistant Dean for Faculty Development Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department DA Student Aff-Medical Position Type Faculty Location Shreveport Description The Assistant Dean for Faculty Development at LSU Health Shreveport School of Medicine, serves the School of Medicine mission to provide professional development activities and opportunities to faculty involved in undergraduate and graduate medical education (UME and GME). Notably, the assistant dean will provide faculty members structured faculty development programming designed to enhance the transference of knowledge, skill and behavior from the educator to the learner. The Assistant Dean for Faculty Development will report directly to the Senior Associate Dean for Medical Education and Administration and work collaboratively to promote an atmosphere of continuous professional development to support an ongoing strategy for faculty development within the School of Medicine. The assistant dean will maintain a customer-oriented awareness in acknowledging and responding to needs as they occur to ensure that satisfaction is met at all times. Essential Functions: Provide key administrative and programmatic development of structured faculty development programs for the school of medicine. Serve as the point of initial contact and primary liaison for the physician leaders and other educators such as designated institutional officials, department chairs, and program directors ensuring that all faculty development needs and requirements for undergraduate and graduate medical education programs are met and addressed in a timely manner. Identify the resources, priorities and infrastructure necessary to advance faculty professional development efforts and opportunities within the school. Lead the office of faculty development in promoting an environment that models excellent effective teamwork, outstanding service, and productivity. Assist in identifying, developing, organizing and implementing structured programing for faculty development for the purpose of enhancing the transference of knowledge, skill and behavior from the educator to the learner such as lectures, workshops, etc. Gather stakeholder(s) to include faculty feedback and data to make programmatic recommendations to senior leadership. Notably, assists in identifying need areas through insight gained from results of faculty educa9onal evaluations in collaboration with respective stakeholders and develops and incorporates programing that address the identified need(s) into program-wide faculty development plans. Coordinate and work with internal and external partners/stakeholders to create, support and facilitate the access and engagement of faculty in faculty development programs toward the advancement of their professional development as educators, clinicians and scientist. Assist in gathering and collating faculty members participation in faculty development programs and activities related to their skills as an educator, clinician, scientist and scholarly activities for accreditation reporting purposes. Create and manage project timelines, monitor and perform necessary tracking and evaluation of the effectiveness of the implemented faculty development programs and activities annually and identify areas of strength and opportunity for improvement. Working with other offices within the school of medicine, assist to compile documents, materials, and records to support the professional development of faculty applications for promotion and tenure to include faculty educational evaluations. Work with Senior Associate Dean for Medical Education and Administration to support ongoing faculty development projects and programs. Regular attendance of the allocated percent effort is required to perform the functions of this position. Perform other related duties and activities, as assigned. Qualifications The applicant must meet the following: A Medical Degree from an accredited university with full ability for a full and unrestricted medical license, and certification by their respective board or accrediting body. Additionally, at least four (4) years of relevant workplace experience in leading professional development activities in an undergraduate and graduate medical education environment and possess a deep familiarity with undergraduate and graduate medical education accreditation requirements as well as, knowledge and the ability to apply learning theories, practices and principles. Demonstrated strong project management, administrative and people-skills expertise with proven track record of contributing to the development and implementation of strategic plans which lead to high performance and transformative change. Demonstrated excellent oral and written communication skills with a verbal capacity to express ideas that engage executive and physician leaders, residents and students to build effective learning environments. Preferred Qualifications Six (6) years of meritorious experience working with faculty, residents and students in a learning environment. Practical experience and skills in the use of common computer software including word processing, spreadsheets, and databases/data entry (MS Word, PowerPoint, Excel, etc.). Additional Position Information Salary Range: Competitive and commensurate with experience Primary Location: Shreveport, LA (On-Site) About the School The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about these benefits. Salary is commensurate with experience and training Generous Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Accidental Death & Dismemberment Insurance Flexible Spending Account Optional Retirement Plans LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Applicant Instructions Locate and click on the Apply Online button located at the bottom of the screen, enter your contact information, and upload your resume/CV. If you are contacted for an interview, please let us know at that time if you will need special accommodations. Apply Online LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. LSU Health Shreveport has a goal of having at least 7% of our workers as people with disabilities. © 2026 LSUHSC Yes No"
    },
    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5888": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor Clinical - Medicine, Hospitalist - MC EA Conway",
      "description": "Assistant Professor Clinical - Medicine, Hospitalist | LSUHSC Shreveport Tuesday, October 13, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Assistant Professor Clinical - Medicine, Hospitalist Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department MC EA Conway Position Type Faculty Location Monroe Description Duties will include providing/supervising Hospital Medicine services to in-patient setting and assist with in-house call to be determined by the Department Chairman along with involvement in other outside institutional endeavors. Also included is teaching/educational obligations throughout your employment. Consideration will be extended to all candidates who meet the required qualifications. Special interest will be directed to candidates who meet or exceed the needs of the department. Family Medicine/Internal Medicine providers are encouraged to apply. Qualifications The applicant must meet the following: MD and/or DO Board certified/eligible in Family Medicine or Internal Medicine Licensed or eligible for licensure in the State of Louisiana A distinguished record in Hospital Medicine Commensurate clinical activities Candidates must have a firm commitment to the education of residents and medical students Additional Position Information PSN/PER Number: PSN 28763/PER 3364 Salary: Commensurate with experience Primary Location: Monroe, LA (On-Site) About the School The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about these benefits. The salary is commensurate with experience and training. Generous Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Accidental Death & Dismemberment Insurance Flexible Spending Account Optional Retirement Plans LSU Health is an equal oppor