    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5917": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Tenure Track - AH Physical Therapy",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Tenure Track | LSUHSC Shreveport Tuesday, October 13, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Assistant Professor - Tenure Track Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department AH Physical Therapy Position Type Faculty Location Shreveport Description Responsibilities (95%) The Department of Physical Therapy at LSU Health Shreveport welcomes applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position to begin teaching classes for the second cohort/second year of our Lafayette Hybrid DPT Program. The faculty member would have primary responsibilities related to establishing a line of research, with the goal of success in peer-reviewed publications and grant funding, in addition to teaching in the hybrid DPT program, which includes advising students and working collaboratively with other members of the programmatic and departmental faculty. Courses with teaching needs currently include: PHTH 7819 Cardiovascular & Pulmonary I, PHTH 7820 Cardiovascular & Pulmonary II, PHTH 7822 Progression of Care, PHTH 7824 Managing Complex Patients, PHTH 7825 Community Needs Assessment and Program Planning, PHTH 7826 Neuromuscular I, and PHTH 7827 Neuromuscular II. All new faculty are paired with a senior faculty member for all assigned teaching assignments for their first two semesters and will only be expected to take on the role as course coordinator in their third semester. The program has a large group of associated faculty members that assist with teaching responsibilities, and all courses have at least two core faculty members assigned, for effective team teaching. The Lafayette Hybrid Program is located in Lafayette, LA, which is three hours south of the main campus located in Shreveport, Louisiana. The program is fully accredited as an expansion of the parent program located in Shreveport. This faculty member would be the third core faculty member for this campus/program, with an additional five core faculty who teach in both the Shreveport Residential and Lafayette Hybrid Programs. The Lafayette Hybrid Program currently has a maximum cohort size of 24 students with state-of-the-art AV and clinical/classroom equipment for laboratory and active-learning-based teaching activities. There is a research laboratory that is currently unfinished, which the faculty member could furnish through grant funds and use for their scholarly pursuits, along with other faculty members. Non-Essential Position Functions & Duties Marginal Functions (5%) Performs other related duties and responsibilities as assigned. Regular attendance is required to perform the functions of this position. The faculty member would be expected to relocate to Lafayette, LA (be a Louisiana resident), or a nearby area within the state, to be on campus during students’ on-campus and remote learning weeks. Incumbent will maintain a customer-oriented awareness in acknowledging and responding to needs as they occur that customer satisfaction is met at all times. Qualifications The applicant must meet the following: Eligibility for licensure as a Physical Therapist in Louisiana. Possess an academic Doctoral Degree (PhD, EdD, DSc, DHS, or equivalent), although candidates in the final year of their dissertation may also be considered. Demonstration of excellence in previous teaching and/or research experience. Ability to work independently toward goals as well as collaborate with faculty, staff, students, and other stakeholders from a diverse background. Preferred Qualifications PhD or EdD with track record of grantsmanship, research, and peer-reviewed publications. Demonstration of experience in hybrid education (didactic and clinical). Board certification in any area of physical therapy is desirable (e.g., neurologic, cardiopulmonary, pelvic health, or pediatrics). Additional Position Information PSN/PER Number: PSN 60091/PER 3777 Salary Range: $90,000 - $110,000 Primary Location: Lafayette, LA About the School The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about these benefits. Salary is commensurate with experience and training Generous Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Accidental Death & Dismemberment Insurance Flexible Spending Account Optional Retirement Plans Applicant Instructions To Apply : Locate and click on the Apply Online button located at the bottom of the screen, enter your contact information, and upload your resume/CV. If you are contacted for an interview, please let us know at that time if you will need special accommodations. Apply Online LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. LSU Health Shreveport has a goal of having at least 7% of our workers as people with disabilities. © 2026 LSUHSC Yes No"
    },
    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5921": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor - Body Radiologist - MC Radiology",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor - Body Radiologist | LSUHSC Shreveport Tuesday, October 13, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Assistant/Associate Professor - Body Radiologist Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department MC Radiology Position Type Faculty Location Shreveport Description The Department of Radiology at Louisiana State University Health Sciences Center in Shreveport is seeking a full-time BC/BE Body Radiologist. Primary responsibilities include patient care, resident education, and medical student education.  Protected time is available to pursue clinical and/or laboratory research interests. Body imaging section includes Abdomen, Chest and Ultrasound. Nuclear Medicine experience is not required but preferred.  Academic rank and salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Through our partnership with Ochsner LSU Health Shreveport and Ochsner LSU Health St. Mary, we provide the only major academic medical center in the area and receive patients from a catchment area with a radius of approximately 75-100 miles which includes a population of approximately 1½ million people. The Radiology Department is a large academic multispecialty Department with active clinical and basic research programs. Shreveport is an attractive, comfortable, small southern city with excellent schools, good restaurants, and multicultural opportunities. It is an excellent place to raise children. Regular attendance is required to perform the functions of this position. The work hours are generally Monday through Friday from 8:00AM to 5:00PM. Qualifications The applicant must meet the following: Board Certified/Board Eligible Body Radiologist Licensed/eligible for Louisiana Medical License Additional Position Information PSN/PER Number: PSN 60121/PER 3288 Salary Range: $113,000 - $140,000 Primary Location: Shreveport, LA (On-Site) About the School The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about these benefits. Salary is commensurate with experience and training Generous Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Accidental Death & Dismemberment Insurance Flexible Spending Account Optional Retirement Plans Applicant Instructions To Apply : Locate and click on the Apply Online button located at the bottom of the screen, enter your contact information, and upload your resume/CV. If you are contacted for an interview, please let us know at that time if you will need special accommodations. Apply Online LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. LSU Health Shreveport has a goal of having at least 7% of our workers as people with disabilities. © 2026 LSUHSC Yes No"
    },
    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5942": {
      "title": "Associate Professor - MB Biochemistry",
      "description": "Associate Professor | LSUHSC Shreveport Tuesday, October 13, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Associate Professor Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department MB Biochemistry Position Type Faculty Location Shreveport Description The Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology at LSU Health Shreveport seeks a highly motivated Associate Professor to develop and maintain an independent, externally funded research program in biochemistry, molecular biology, cancer biology, or related biomedical sciences. The successful candidate will contribute to graduate and medical education, mentor trainees, and participate in departmental, institutional, and professional service activities. Essential Duties and Responsibilities • Maintain an active, nationally recognized, externally funded research program. • Publish high-impact scholarly work in peer-reviewed journals. • Teach and participate in medical, graduate, and/or postgraduate education programs. • Mentor graduate students, postdoctoral fellows, residents, and other trainees. • Collaborate with faculty across departments and research centers. • Serve on departmental, institutional, and professional committees. • Contribute to the growth of the research and educational missions of LSU Health Shreveport. Qualifications The applicant must meet the following: • Ph.D., M.D., or equivalent doctoral degree in Biochemistry, Molecular Biology, Cancer Biology, or a related biomedical discipline. • Eligible for appointment at the rank of Associate Professor. • Demonstrated record of independent research productivity. • Evidence of successful extramural funding or strong potential for sustained external funding. • Record of publications in peer-reviewed scientific journals. • Experience teaching and mentoring students and/or trainees. Preferred Qualifications • Active federal or equivalent peer-reviewed research funding. • Expertise in cancer biology, translational research, or related areas aligned with institutional priorities. • Demonstrated experience in interdisciplinary and collaborative research. • Strong commitment to mentorship and academic service. Additional Position Information PSN/PER Number: PSN 60193/PER 4117 Salary Range: $130,000 - $170,000 Primary Location: Shreveport, LA (On-Site) About the School The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about these benefits. • Salary is commensurate with experience and training • Generous Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance • Life Insurance • Long-Term Disability Insurance • Accidental Death & Dismemberment Insurance • Flexible Spending Account • Optional Retirement Plans Applicant Instructions To Apply: Locate and click on the Apply Online button located at the bottom of the screen, enter your contact information, and upload your resume/CV. If you are contacted for an interview, please let us know at that time if you will need special accommodations. Apply Online LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. LSU Health Shreveport has a goal of having at least 7% of our workers as people with disabilities. © 2026 LSUHSC Yes No"
