    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5955": {
      "title": "Professor - MB Biochemistry",
      "description": "Professor | LSUHSC Shreveport Tuesday, October 13, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Professor Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department MB Biochemistry Position Type Faculty Location Shreveport Description The Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology at LSU Health Shreveport seeks an accomplished and highly motivated faculty member at the rank of Professor to provide senior academic leadership and maintain a nationally recognized, externally funded research program in biochemistry, molecular biology, cancer biology, or related biomedical sciences. The successful candidate will demonstrate a sustained record of scholarly productivity, extramural funding, teaching excellence, mentorship, and academic service. The Professor will contribute to graduate and medical education, mentor junior faculty and trainees, foster interdisciplinary collaboration, and support the continued growth of the research and educational missions of LSU Health Shreveport. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Maintain and further develop a nationally recognized, independent, externally funded research program appropriate for appointment at the rank of Professor. Demonstrate sustained scholarly productivity through high-quality peer-reviewed publications and contributions to biochemistry, molecular biology, cancer biology, or related biomedical sciences. Provide leadership in research program development, interdisciplinary collaboration, and strategic initiatives within the department and institution. Teach and contribute to medical, graduate, and/or postgraduate education programs. Mentor graduate students, postdoctoral fellows, residents, junior faculty, and other trainees. Participate actively in departmental, institutional, and professional service, including committee leadership and peer-review activities as appropriate. Contribute to the advancement of LSU Health Shreveport’s research, education, mentorship, and service missions. Qualifications Ph.D., M.D., or equivalent doctoral degree in Biochemistry, Molecular Biology, Cancer Biology, or a closely related biomedical discipline. Credentials and experience appropriate for appointment at the rank of Professor, consistent with institutional criteria. Established national or international reputation in an area of biochemistry, molecular biology, cancer biology, or related biomedical sciences. Sustained record of independent research productivity, including impactful peer-reviewed publications. Demonstrated history of obtaining extramural research funding or equivalent evidence of sustained externally supported research activity. Documented experience in teaching, mentoring, and academic service. Evidence of leadership in research, education, service, program development, or collaborative academic initiatives. Preferred Qualifications Active federal or equivalent peer-reviewed research funding. Research expertise aligned with institutional priorities, including cancer biology, translational research, molecular mechanisms of disease, immunology, metabolism, or related areas. Demonstrated ability to lead collaborative, multidisciplinary research programs. Strong record of mentoring junior faculty, graduate students, postdoctoral fellows, and other trainees. Commitment to academic leadership, institutional service, education, mentorship, and professional engagement. Additional Position Information PSN/PER Number: PSN 60217/PER 4118 Salary Range: Competitive and commensurate with experience Primary Location: Shreveport, LA (On-Site) About the School The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about these benefits. Salary is commensurate with experience and training Generous Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Accidental Death & Dismemberment Insurance Flexible Spending Account Optional Retirement Plans Applicant Instructions To Apply : Locate and click on the Apply Online button located at the bottom of the screen, enter your contact information, and upload your resume/CV. If you are contacted for an interview, please let us know at that time if you will need special accommodations. Apply Online LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. LSU Health Shreveport has a goal of having at least 7% of our workers as people with disabilities. © 2026 LSUHSC Yes No"
    },
    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5961": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor - Pediatric Urologist - MC Urology",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor - Pediatric Urologist | LSUHSC Shreveport Tuesday, October 13, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Assistant/Associate Professor - Pediatric Urologist Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department MC Urology Position Type Faculty Location Shreveport Description The Department of Urology at Louisiana State University Health Sciences Center in Shreveport is seeking a full-time BC/BE Urologist to expand its full-time clinical faculty. Must be BE/BC in Urology and eligible for LA Medical license. Primary responsibilities include patient care, resident education, and medical student education.  Clinical duties and responsibilities rotate among our tertiary Ochsner LSU Health Shreveport Academic Medical Center and two affiliated teaching institutions. Several da Vinci surgical systems (including a dual-console unit) are available for patient care and resident training. The successful applicant will join several full-time faculty members in a fully accredited Urology Residency Training Program. Academic rank and salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Ochsner LSU Health Shreveport, in conjunction with Ochsner LSU Health St. Mary, is the only major academic medical center in the area and receives patients from a catchment area with a radius of approximately 75-100 miles which includes a population of approximately 1½ million people. Shreveport is an attractive, comfortable, small southern city with excellent schools, good restaurants, and multicultural opportunities. It is an excellent place to raise children. The LSU Systems Office has provided LSUHSC-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about these benefits. Regular attendance is required to perform the functions of this position.  The work hours are generally Monday through Friday from 8:30AM to 5:00PM. Qualifications The applicant must meet the following: Must be BE/BC in Pediatric Urology and eligible for LA Medical license. Additional Position Information PSN/PER Number: PSN 60239/PER 22-09-8648 Salary Range: Competitive and commensurate with experience Primary Location: Shreveport, LA (On-Site) About the School The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about these benefits. Salary is commensurate with experience and training Generous Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Accidental Death & Dismemberment Insurance Flexible Spending Account Optional Retirement Plans Applicant Instructions To Apply : Locate and click on the Apply Online button located at the bottom of the screen, enter your contact information, and upload your resume/CV. If you are contacted for an interview, please let us know at that time if you will need special accommodations. Apply Online LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. LSU Health Shreveport has a goal of having at least 7% of our workers as people with disabilities. © 2026 LSUHSC Yes No"
    },
    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5968": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Professor - AH Physical Therapy",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate/Professor | LSUHSC Shreveport Tuesday, October 13, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Assistant/Associate/Professor Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department AH Physical Therapy Position Type Faculty Location Shreveport Description The Department of Physical Therapy at LSU Health Shreveport welcomes applications for a tenure-track open rank faculty position. The faculty member would have primary responsibilities related to establishing a line of research, with the goal of success in peer-reviewed publications and grant funding. The faculty member would also have teaching responsibilities in our Shreveport Residential DPT Program, depending on their area of expertise. Teaching requirements include advising students and working collaboratively with other members of the programmatic and departmental faculty. There is flexibility in potential teaching assignments depending on the candidate’s interest and expertise, but current teaching needs include, but are not limited to, neuroscience/neurologic rehabilitation and medical conditions/other systems. Current research initiatives within the department include rural education workforce initiatives, human performance (heat stress, biomechanics, etc.), and population health (geriatrics, balance issues, cancer, and neurologic conditions). Additional opportunities may include teaching PhD in Rehab Sciences program in which this new faculty member can teach, mentor, and serve on committees, along with a gait lab and developing human performance lab. The Shreveport Residential Program is located at our main campus in Shreveport, LA, where this faculty member will be based. The program is fully accredited. The program has a maximum cohort size of 36 students. We have a fully operational faculty clinic on the ground floor of the School where the faculty can practice a portion of their time and/or recruit study subjects. This area also houses our orthopaedic and neurologic physical therapy residency programs. Our department also includes our Lafayette Hybrid Program in Lafayette, LA, which is three hours south of the main campus located in Shreveport, Louisiana. The program is fully accredited as an expansion of the parent program located in Shreveport. The Lafayette Hybrid Program currently has a maximum cohort size of 24 students. However, it is expected that this faculty member will primary have a teaching role in our Shreveport Residential Program. Qualifications The applicant must meet the following: Eligibility for licensure as a physical therapist in Louisiana Possess an academic doctoral degree (PhD, EdD, DSc, DHS, or equivalent), although candidates in the final year of their dissertation may also be considered Demonstration of excellence in previous teaching and/or research experience Ability to work independently toward goals as well as collaborate with faculty, staff, students, and other stakeholders from a diverse background. Preferred Qualifications PhD or EdD with track record of grantsmanship, research, and peer-reviewed publications Demonstration of experience in teaching (didactic and clinical) Board certification in any area of physical therapy is desirable, but neurologic or pediatric specialists are encouraged to apply. Additional Position Information PSN/PER Number: PSN 49821/PER 4377 Salary Range: $110,000-132,000 Primary Location: Shreveport, LA (On-Site) About the School The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about these benefits. Salary is commensurate with experience and training Generous Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Accidental Death & Dismemberment Insurance Flexible Spending Account Optional Retirement Plans Applicant Instructions To Apply : Locate and click on the Apply Online button located at the bottom of the screen, enter your contact information, and upload your resume/CV. If you are contacted for an interview, please let us know at that time if you will need special accommodations. Apply Online LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. LSU Health Shreveport has a goal of having at least 7% of our workers as people with disabilities. © 2026 LSUHSC Yes No"
    },
    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5969": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - AH Physical Therapy",
      "description": "Assistant Professor | LSUHSC Shreveport Tuesday, October 13, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Assistant Professor Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department AH Physical Therapy Position Type Faculty Location Shreveport Description The Department of Physical Therapy at LSU Health Shreveport welcomes applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position. The faculty member would have primary responsibilities related to establishing a line of research, with the goal of success in peer-reviewed publications and grant funding. The faculty member would also have teaching responsibilities in our Shreveport Residential DPT Program, and our Lafayette Hybrid Program depending on their area of expertise. Teaching requirements include advising students and working collaboratively with other members of the programmatic and departmental faculty. There is flexibility in potential teaching assignments depending on the candidate’s interest and expertise, but current teaching needs include, but are not limited to, neurologic and pediatric populations, pharmacology, patient assessment and treatment prescription, foundational patient management skills, and medical screening (i.e., radiology, laboratory medicine, etc.). Current research initiatives within the department include rural education workforce initiatives, human performance (heat stress, biomechanics, etc.), and population health (geriatrics, balance issues, cancer, and neurologic conditions). Additional opportunities may include teaching PhD in Rehab Sciences program in which this new faculty member can teach, mentor, and serve on committees, along with a gait lab and developing human performance lab. The Shreveport Residential Program is located at our main campus in Shreveport, LA, where his faculty member will be based. The program is fully accredited. The program has a maximum cohort size of 36 students. We have a fully operational faculty clinic on the ground floor of the School where the faculty can practice a portion of their time and/or recruit study subjects. This area also houses our orthopaedic and neurologic physical therapy residency programs. The Lafayette Hybrid Program is in Lafayette, LA, which is three hours south of the main campus located in Shreveport, Louisiana. The program is fully accredited as an expansion of the parent program located in Shreveport. The Lafayette Hybrid Program currently has a maximum cohort size of 24 students with state-of-the-art AV and clinical/classroom equipment for laboratory and active-learning-based teaching activities. The majority of any potential teaching efforts in this program could be done remotely from Shreveport. Regular attendance is required to perform the functions of this position. The faculty member would be expected to relocate to Shreveport, LA (be a Louisiana resident), or a nearby area within the state. Qualifications The applicant must meet the following: Eligibility for licensure as a physical therapist in Louisiana Possess an academic doctoral degree (PhD, EdD, DSc, DHS, or equivalent), although candidates in the final year of their dissertation may also be considered Demonstration of excellence in previous teaching and/or research experience Ability to work independently toward goals as well as collaborate with faculty, staff, students, and other stakeholders from a diverse background. Preferred Qualifications PhD or EdD with track record of grantsmanship, research, and peer-reviewed publications Demonstration of experience in hybrid education (didactic and clinical) Board certification in any area of physical therapy is desirable, but neurologic or pediatrics is preferred. Additional Position Information PSN/PER Number: PSN 56814/PER 4390 Salary Range: $110,000-$119,000 Primary Location: Shreveport, LA (On-Site) About the School The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about these benefits. Salary is commensurate with experience and training Generous Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Accidental Death & Dismemberment Insurance Flexible Spending Account Optional Retirement Plans Applicant Instructions To Apply : Locate and click on the Apply Online button located at the bottom of the screen, enter your contact information, and upload your resume/CV. If you are contacted for an interview, please let us know at that time if you will need special accommodations. Apply Online LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. LSU Health Shreveport has a goal of having at least 7% of our workers as people with disabilities. © 2026 LSUHSC Yes No"
    },
    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5970": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Biochemistry and Molecular Biology - MB Biochemistry",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Biochemistry and Molecular Biology | LSUHSC Shreveport Tuesday, October 13, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Assistant Professor - Biochemistry and Molecular Biology Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department MB Biochemistry Position Type Faculty Location Shreveport Description The Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology at LSU Health Shreveport seeks a highly motivated faculty member at the rank of Assistant Professor to develop and maintain an independent, externally funded research program in biochemistry, molecular biology, metabolism, cancer biology, or related biomedical sciences. The successful candidate will contribute to graduate and medical education, mentor trainees, participate in departmental, institutional, and professional service activities, and support the research and educational missions of LSU Health Shreveport. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Develop, maintain, or expand an active, independent, externally funded research program appropriate to faculty rank. Publish scholarly work in peer-reviewed journals and contribute to the advancement of biochemistry, molecular biology, cancer biology, or related biomedical sciences. Teach and participate in medical, graduate, and/or postgraduate education programs. Mentor graduate students, postdoctoral fellows, residents, and other trainees. Collaborate with faculty across departments, research centers, and institutional programs. Serve on departmental, institutional, and professional committees as appropriate to rank and experience. Contribute to the continued growth of the research and educational missions of LSU Health Shreveport. Qualifications The applicant must meet the following: Ph.D., M.D., or equivalent doctoral degree in Biochemistry, Molecular Biology, Cancer Biology, or a related biomedical discipline. Eligible for appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor, based on qualifications, experience, and institutional criteria. Evidence of strong research training, scholarly productivity, and clear potential to establish an independent, externally funded research program. Record of publications in peer-reviewed scientific journals appropriate to career stage. Experience or demonstrated potential in teaching, mentoring, and academic service. Preferred Qualifications Current extramural NIH funding, preferably at the R01 level; exceptional candidates holding a NIH K99/R00 or comparable career-development award are encouraged to apply. Expertise in cancer biology, translational research, molecular mechanisms of disease, immunology, or related areas aligned with institutional priorities. Demonstrated or emerging experience in interdisciplinary and collaborative research. Strong commitment to mentorship, education, academic service, and institutional citizenship. Additional Position Information PSN/PER Number: PSN 60265 & 60266/PER 4116 Salary Range: Competitive and commensurate with experience Primary Location: Shreveport, LA (On-Site) About the School The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about these benefits. Salary is commensurate with experience and training Generous Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Accidental Death & Dismemberment Insurance Flexible Spending Account Optional Retirement Plans Applicant Instructions To Apply : Locate and click on the Apply Online button located at the bottom of the screen, enter your contact information, and upload your resume/CV. If you are contacted for an interview, please let us know at that time if you will need special accommodations. Apply Online LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. LSU Health Shreveport has a goal of having at least 7% of our workers as people with disabilities. © 2026 LSUHSC Yes No"
    },
    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5974": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor - Tenure Track - MC Pathology",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor - Tenure Track | LSUHSC Shreveport Friday, October 16, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Assistant/Associate Professor - Tenure Track Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department MC Pathology Position Type Faculty Location Shreveport Description The Department of Pathology and Translational Pathobiology at LSU Health Shreveport invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant or Associate Professor level. We seek a scientist with a Ph.D., M.D., or M.D./Ph.D., postdoctoral training, and a strong record of research productivity, including current or emerging R01- or K99/R00-level funding, to develop an innovative and independently funded research program in cardiovascular or cancer biology. Although the search is open at all ranks, the primary emphasis is on recruiting an outstanding assistant professor-level investigator. The Department of Pathology and Translational Pathobiology is a central driver of research growth at LSU Health Shreveport, with expanding faculty programs and strong institutional investment in biomedical research. The department leads the institution in extramural funding and supports a highly collaborative environment spanning cardiovascular disease, metabolism, and inflammation. We are particularly interested in candidates building research programs that intersect with institutional strengths in cardiovascular and cancer biology, including cardiometabolism, cardio-oncology, and cancer metabolism. LSU Health Shreveport provides a collaborative academic medical center environment with strong infrastructure and institutional support for research development and faculty success.  Faculty benefit from collaborative opportunities through major center-level programs, including the NIH-funded CoBRE Center for Redox Biology and Cardiovascular Disease and the NSF EPSCoR CREST Center for Post-Transcriptional Regulation. These programs provide access to shared core facilities supporting molecular signaling, analytical redox biology, genotyping, animal phenotyping, metabolomics, and iPSC-based model systems, enabling a wide range of mechanistic and translational research.  Additional collaborative opportunities are available through the Center for Cardiovascular Diseases and Sciences and the Feist-Weiller Cancer Center, which support local research through pilot funding, shared resources, and access to clinical collaborations. Qualifications The applicant must meet the following: • Ph.D., M.D., or M.D./Ph.D. • Postdoctoral Training • Strong record of research productivity, including current or emerging R01- or K99/R00-level funding Preferred Qualifications Assistant professor-level investigator Additional Position Information PSN/PER Number: PSN 60278/PER 4410 Salary Range: Competitive and commensurate with experience Primary Location: Shreveport, LA (On-Site) About the School The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about these benefits. Salary is commensurate with experience and training Generous Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Accidental Death & Dismemberment Insurance Flexible Spending Account Optional Retirement Plans Applicant Instructions To Apply : Applicants should send a cover letter, curriculum vitae, research statement, funding statement, teaching statement, and contact information for three references to: Wayne Orr, Ph.D. Vice Chair for Research, Department of Pathology and Translational Pathobiology Director, Center for Cardiovascular Diseases and Sciences LSU Health Shreveport wayne.orr@lsuhs.edu ShvFacultyRecruitment@lsuhs.edu Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. If you are contacted for an interview, please let us know at that time if you will need special accommodations. Apply Online LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. LSU Health Shreveport has a goal of having at least 7% of our workers as people with disabilities. © 2026 LSUHSC Yes No"
    },
    "https://www.lsuhsc.edu/shv/CareerOpportunities/Home/Detail/5987": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - MC EA Conway",
      "description": "Assistant Professor | LSUHSC Shreveport Wednesday, October 28, 2026 Login / Register FAQ Contact Us Open Positions Assistant Professor Position Details Expiration Date Open Until Filled Department MC EA Conway Position Type Faculty Location Monroe Description Duties will include providing/supervising Pulmonary services to in-patient and outpatient setting and assist with in-house call to be determined by the Department Chairman along with involvement in other outside institutional endeavors. Also included is teaching/educational obligations throughout your employment. Consideration will be extended to all candidates who meet the required qualifications. Special interest will be directed to candidates who meet or exceed the needs of the department. Qualifications The applicant must meet the following: MD and/or DO Board certified/eligible in Internal Medicine/Pulmonology Licensed or eligible for licensure in the State of Louisiana A distinguished record in Pulmonology Commensurate clinical activities Candidates must have a firm commitment to the education of residents and medical students Additional Position Information PSN/PER Number: PSN 60302/PER 3449 Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Primary Location: Monroe, LA (On-Site) About the School The LSU Systems Office has provided LSU Health-Shreveport employees with excellent benefit options designed with you and your dependents in mind. Our Benefits Section is available between 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, to help answer any questions you might have about these benefits. The salary is commensurate with experience and training. Generous Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Accidental Death & Dismemberment Insurance Flexible Spending Account Optional Retirement Plans LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Applicant Instructions To Apply : Locate and click on the Apply Online button located at the bottom of the screen, enter your contact information, and upload your resume/CV. If you are contacted for an interview, please let us know at that time if you will need special accommodations. Apply Online LSU Health is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. LSU Health Shreveport has a goal of having at least 7% of our workers as people with disabilities. © 2026 LSUHSC Yes No"
    }
